      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Based on these two snippets, the pattern appears to be a rhetorical transition mechanism rather than a discrete code. In both cases, using \"resilience\" followed by \"contingency\" functions as a formalized preamble that frames the necessity of the upcoming policy change. This pairing signals to the audience that the administration has anticipated risk and is therefore prepared to implement the stated solution. It functions as a verbal cue, moving from abstract preparedness to concrete action.",
